#
# ChkTeX configuration for the sources of the paper, the report and the slides.
#
# Every suppression below names the constructs in these documents that trigger
# its warning, as ChkTeX 1.7.9 of TeX Live 2026 reports them for each file and
# in the one run over all files that `make check` makes; where no construct
# triggers a warning at present, its line says so. Anything not listed stays
# active, so the lint is a gate (`make check`), not a formality. The sources of
# the report keep the text of its revised edition and are not edited to please
# the lint. Warning numbers are those of the ChkTeX manual.
#
# In one run over several files, ChkTeX keeps its math mode from one file to
# the next. The $1 in the replacement strings of the biblatex source maps in
# report/report.tex switches it on, so ChkTeX reads the rest of that file, and
# in `make check` the files of slides/ after it, as math (warnings 16, 25, 35).

CmdLine
{
    -n1   # a command followed by a space: the \iffirst... conditionals of the
          # acronym macros in paper.tex, commands at a line end such as
          # \raggedbottom, \titlepage and the \endhead of longtable, and
          # \allowbreak, \dotsep and \textquotesingle before text
    -n2   # citations in the table cells of Table 5.2 are not tied to a word
    -n6   # the \itshape of the comment style of the listings in paper.tex, whose
          # group closes without an italic correction
    -n8   # hyphens in part, standard and ISSN numbers such as MF0207FTE52-1K and
          # EN 50121-3-2, -- for ranges and empty table cells, and the spaced
          # hyphen of the YAML test name Geber 3 - I in the deck
    -n9   # the run-in headings 1) to 3) of Section IV-B in paper.tex: ChkTeX
          # expects the } of \textbf and finds their )
    -n10  # the same headings: ChkTeX then takes the } of \textbf for a solo }
    -n12  # a full stop before a command that begins the next sentence, such as
          # \gls, \enquote, \emph or \href, which ChkTeX takes for the end of an
          # abbreviation, and the abbreviation Periph. in a table of the paper
    -n13  # a capital letter before a full stop, a colon or a semicolon: sentences
          # that end on an acronym (CPU., ROM.), and FPGA; or Annex~F: in the text
    -n16  # the $1 of the source maps in report.tex leaves ChkTeX in math mode at
          # the end of that file
    -n17  # the run-in headings 1) to 3) of Section IV-B in paper.tex close a
          # parenthesis that they do not open
    -n18  # straight double quotes where they belong: the YAML strings of the
          # Layer 2 frame of the deck, the string delimiter of the YAML language
          # of the listings in paper.tex, and an inch mark in Appendix B
    -n24  # \label stands on its own line after a sectioning command or a caption
    -n25  # underscores that ChkTeX in math mode (see -n16) takes for subscripts:
          # the logo file name in report.tex and, in `make check`, the YAML keys
          # and capture file names of the deck
    -n29  # an x between digits that is no product: the 0x7cd of the e-mail and
          # web addresses in the author note of paper.tex and of the address in
          # report/meta/author/mail.tex, and pin-header sizes such as 1x6 and
          # 2x8 in the bill of materials of Appendix B
    -n35  # words that contain log, ln or Pr, such as log and logging, which
          # ChkTeX in math mode (see -n16) takes for \log, \ln and \Pr: in
          # report.tex and, in `make check`, in the deck and the handout
    -n36  # no space before an opening parenthesis: the list labels (\alph*) and
          # (\arabic*) of paper.tex and of the report abstracts, Designator(s)
          # in the bill of materials, and the regular expressions of the source
          # maps in report.tex
    -n38  # no construct triggers it at present under ChkTeX's default logical
          # quote style; the traditional style would flag the string delimiter
          # ' of the YAML language in paper.tex and two notes of the deck that
          # close a quotation before a comma or a full stop
    -n44  # the user rule against vertical rules misreads @{}l@{} column specifications
}
